{"kind":"request","text":"Claude: make docs/getting-started.md actually get a person to a running workroom. Refiled from 34e05695, which I rested on my identity-lane promise by mistake; this one rests on assert ca4a15a4, the durable record of what Hugh asked for. The work is unchanged.\n\nWHAT IS MISSING, IN ORDER. Initialise the workroom. Add three agent actors -- planner, builder and checker, or names of that shape, so the reader sees a roster with more than one agent in it and can tell which one they are talking to. Install an MCP for each actor, with worked examples for both codex and claude-code, because \"install an MCP\" is where a first-time reader stops. Then start a coding session per actor, each with its own loop prompt naming its own MCP.\n\nHugh gave the prompt shape he wants shown, substituting the right MCP name per session:\n\n  Using the gitseq workroom skill and 'builder' MCP, check for work items and\n  prioritize appropriately to keep progressing. Dispatch tasks to subagents.\n  Continue checking every 10 minutes indefinitely.\n\nTake that as the intent, not as bytes to transcribe: he typed \"worksoom\", and the page should say workroom. Keep it close to the README's prompt, or say plainly why a modified version is better for a first run.\n\nTHE BAR IS THAT IT WORKS. Run every command in a scratch directory as a reader would, from an empty directory to three agents polling, and fix the page where it does not. A getting-started page that has not been executed start to finish is a guess. Plain English per ISO 24495-1, for a technical audience.\n\nRest the artifact on the behaviour artifacts for the commands you document -- the actor and MCP surfaces you name -- and not only on the promise, or nothing about the page can ever flare when those move. There is no live artifact at docs/getting-started.md today, so publishing one is part of the job rather than a succession you inherit.","body":{"branch":"request/getting-started-first-use","conditions":"Rewrite or extend docs/getting-started.md so a person with an empty directory reaches a workroom with three agent actors polling for work. It must cover, in order: (1) initialising the workroom; (2) adding three agent actors -- planner, builder, checker or equivalent -- and showing the resulting roster; (3) installing an MCP per actor, with a worked example for codex AND a worked example for claude-code, including how each session ends up bound to its own actor identity; (4) starting one coding session per actor with a loop prompt naming that actor's MCP, close to the README prompt, spelled 'workroom'. Execute every command in a scratch directory from empty to three polling agents before publishing, and fix the page wherever the executed path differs from the written one; say in the report what you ran. Plain English per ISO 24495-1 for a technical audience. Publish the exact-head artifact at docs/getting-started.md resting on the live behaviour artifacts for the surfaces the page documents, not only on the promise. Request independent review from codex or planner with Architecture, Security and Simplification conclusions.","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}